description:
Design a glitch filter that processes a digital input signal to eliminate brief high pulses (glitches) shorter than a specified duration threshold (t). The module counts the length of time the input signal is high, and only outputs a high signal when the input remains high for a period equal to or greater than this threshold. If the input signal goes low before meeting the threshold duration, the output is set to low, effectively filtering out undesired short glitches. This implementation uses a counter and a duration register to accurately measure the input signal's duration across clock cycles.
