description:
Design a circuit that converts a 4-bit binary number to its corresponding 4-bit Gray code representation. The output Gray code is generated by applying the exclusive OR operation between specific bits of the binary input, ensuring that only one bit changes between consecutive values, which is the hallmark of Gray code.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] binary_input,
    output reg [3:0] gray_output
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] binary_input,
    output reg [3:0] gray_output
);always @(*) begin
        gray_output[0] = binary_input[0];
        gray_output[1] = binary_input[0] ^ binary_input[1];
        gray_output[2] = binary_input[1] ^ binary_input[2];
        gray_output[3] = binary_input[2] ^ binary_input[3];
    end

endmodule

