Design a circuit that computes a 64-bit CRC (Cyclic Redundancy Check) value based on an input clock. On each rising edge of the clock, the circuit shifts the current CRC value left by one bit. If the most significant bit of the CRC is 1, it performs an XOR operation with a predefined polynomial (0x9B). The resulting CRC value is then added to the output register, which holds the final computed CRC result.
