Design a barrel shifter that takes an 8-bit input and shifts it to the left by a specified number of positions, defined by a 3-bit shift_amount input. Depending on the value of shift_amount, the circuit outputs the original data shifted left, combining the retained bits with zeros on the right. This allows for efficient bit manipulation in applications such as data processing and digital signal manipulation.
