description:
Design a circuit that converts a 4-bit binary input to a Binary-Coded Decimal (BCD) output. The module checks if the input binary value is less than 10 (4'b1010); if true, it directly maps the binary value to the lower 4 bits of the BCD output, setting the highest bit (thousands place) to 0. If the input binary is 10 or greater, it subtracts 10 from the input and sets the highest bit of the BCD output to 1, effectively representing the BCD equivalent of the input binary value.
module top_module(input wire[3:0] bin,output reg[4:0] BCD
    );

