description:
Design a circular shift register known as a ring counter with a specified number of bits (n). On each positive clock edge, the ring counter shifts its state, moving the last bit to the front while retaining the other bits in their respective positions. The output presents the current state with the least significant bit always set to 0, effectively creating a cyclic pattern across the outputs.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output [n-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output [n-1:0] out
);parameter n = 4; // number of output signals

reg [n-1:0] state;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  state <= {state[n-2:0], state[n-1]};
end

assign out = {1'b0, state[n-2:0]};

endmodule

