Design a 16-bit arithmetic and logic unit (ALU) that performs various operations based on a 4-bit operation code (opc) and two 16-bit input operands (regA and regB). The ALU supports addition, subtraction, multiplication, bitwise operations (AND, OR, XOR), shifting (left, right), and comparison operations, with results stored in output registers (regR and regO). The ALU operates synchronously with a clock signal and can reset to an initial state. The output control signal (CC) indicates the result of the comparison operations. The module incorporates functionality to manage operational phases using the pha input to define data transfer between internal registers and the outputs.
