Write a Verilog module for a 6-bit down counter with asynchronous reset. When reset is high, the counter should reset to 6'b111111. Otherwise, it should count down by one on each clock edge.
module down_counter (
    input clk,
    input reset,
    output reg [5:0] count
);

code:
module down_counter (
    input clk,
    input reset,
    output reg [5:0] count
);always @(posedge clk or posedge reset) begin
        if (reset)
            count <= 6'b111111;
        else
            count <= count - 1;
    end

endmodule

